course: dictionary
lesson: 49
title: Many meanings of account
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word account has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «If a card is lost, the bank can freeze or block it at once, so the money in the account stays safe.» The bank and the money tell you this is a bank account, where a bank looks after your money.
explain: «Using a parent's account to buy something without asking is taking their money.» Here the clue is the buying and the password-style use. An account on a website or game is your name and password for logging in. Ask yourself: what meaning fits here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: An account can also be a report or story of what happened, as in give an account of a trip. Different accounts of the same event can disagree, so a good reader checks more than one.
fact: An account can be a description or story of what happened: an account of the trip.
fact: A bank account is where a bank keeps your money and records what goes in and out.
fact: An account is also your name and password for a website, game or app.
fact: To account for something means to explain it, or to be part of a total: girls account for half the class.
fact: On account of means because of.
exercise: «If a card is lost, the bank can freeze or block it at once, so the money in the account stays safe.» In this sentence, what is the account? | A password for a game | *A bank account, where a bank keeps your money | An explanation of a sum | A story of what happened on a trip
exercise: Lily's friend asks, «Can I use your account to play the game?» Lily says no. What does account mean here? | A report of what happened | A bank account with money in it | *A name and password for logging into a game | A total made of parts
exercise: Girls account for half the class. What does account for mean here? | Keep the money safe | *Are a part of the total | Explain why they left | Tell a story about them
test: «Using a parent's account to buy something without asking is taking their money.» Why is this wrong? | Because accounts are always free | *Because it spends their money without asking | Because the account is a story | Because parents never buy things
test: Two people give different accounts of the same football match. What does account mean here? | A bank where money is kept | A total of something | *A report or story of what happened | A password for a website
exam: Which sentence uses account to mean a bank account? | Two people gave different accounts of the same match | Girls account for half the class | Noah's account posted a silly message in a chat | *Paying money in makes the balance in the account bigger
